<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Morean War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1684–1699</span> · Also known as Sixth Ottoman–Venetian War · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-turkish-war">Great Turkish War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Morean War was the war of 1684–1699 between the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>, part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-turkish-war">Great Turkish War</a>. Venetian forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francesco-morosini">Francesco Morosini</a> conquered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a> (the Morea) between 1685 and 1687 and briefly took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a>, where a shell exploded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthenon">Parthenon</a> in 1687. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-karlowitz">Treaty of Karlowitz</a> in 1699 confirmed Venice's hold on the Morea, which the Ottomans retook in 1715.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/morean-war.jpg" alt="Morean War" width="320" height="158" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Georg Hautsch II · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Medal_for_the_Venetian_victories_in_the_Morean_War,_G._Hautsch,_Nuremberg,_1687.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
